{"name":"Greenfinch","hex":"#bda928","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"greenfinch","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any bird within the genus Chloris (formerly a subset of the genus Carduelis), small passerine songbirds with yellow-green plumage, found throughout Eurasia.\n\nEuropean greenfinch, a common Old World finch (Chloris chloris, syn. Carduelis chloris, Fringilla Chloris), mainly green with yellow in the wings and tail.","European greenfinch, a common Old World finch (Chloris chloris, syn. Carduelis chloris, Fringilla Chloris), mainly green with yellow in the wings and tail."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/greenfinch"}],"entries":[{"title":"Greenfinch","blocks":[{"text":"The greenfinches are small passerine birds in the genus Chloris in the subfamily Carduelinae within the Fringillidae. The species have a Eurasian distribution except for the European greenfinch, which also occurs in North Africa."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Chloris_chloris_%28profile%29.jpg/330px-Chloris_chloris_%28profile%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greenfinch","wikidata":"Q9189957"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Chloris_ambigua%2C_captive.jpg/120px-Chloris_ambigua%2C_captive.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Chloris_ambigua%2C_captive.jpg/250px-Chloris_ambigua%2C_captive.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Chloris_ambigua%2C_captive.jpg/120px-Chloris_ambigua%2C_captive.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChloris_ambigua%2C_captive.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia